{:id :EACL-FORMAL-024
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace
 "materialized-reference/two-singleton-fixed-point-rounds/max-queued-work-1"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 formal model before instantaneous queue-gauge correction"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "RecursiveEngine.dfy accumulated the cardinality of every fixed-point queue round into queuedWork and compared that request counter with :max-queued-work. Production and the generated indexed engine correctly enforce :max-queued-work against instantaneous pending queue depth. Two sequential singleton rounds were therefore rejected by the materialized formal evaluator even though the queue never exceeded one."
 :fix
 "The materialized model now treats queuedWork as the maximum observed pending-work cardinality, checks the current queue cardinality directly against maxQueuedWork, and retains cumulative enqueue accounting as a separate resource dimension outside this safety limit."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.formal.production-kernel-test/generated-materialized-queue-limit-is-instantaneous"
  "eacl.formal.production-kernel-test/datascript-public-recursive-cache-modes-compare-generated-javascript"
  "formal mutation :materialized-queue-limit-counts-cumulative-enqueues"]}
